{"ts": "2026-10-27T15:22:43.762006Z", "run_id": "r-20261027T1517Z-7f3e", "unit": "openspec:add-audit-chain", "seq": 35, "type": "task.started", "task": "4.1", "title": "4.1 Write `src/audit/append.test.ts` first (the scenarios \"First and second event\", \"One clock read per append\", \"Rollback leaves no gap\", \"Wrong or missing tenant context\", \"An invalid event writes nothing\" and \"Month boundary and DEFAULT\"; \"One clock read per append\" uses a clock object whose `now()` returns `2031-03-31T12:00:00.000Z` plus one more millisecond on each call; the stored rows are read through `withTenantTx(db.appPool, ...)`; the \"no tenant set\" case uses `db.appPool.connect()` and `BEGIN` with no `set_config`; the fake `tx` is `{ query: async () => { throw Object.assign(new Error(\"x\"), { code: \"57014\" }) } }`), then implement `AppendOptions`, `appendAudit` in `src/audit/append.ts`, exported through `src/audit/index.ts`. Steps, all through `tx.query`: `validateEvent(event)` first, then `const at = (opts?.clock ?? systemClock).now()`, called exactly once per append, and `formatAt(at)` (no SQL on failure); `SELECT nullif(current_setting('app.tenant_id', true), '') AS t` must equal `ctx.tenantId`, else `AUDIT_CONTEXT_MISMATCH` (`differs` or `unset`); `SELECT seq::text AS seq_text, hash FROM ursitoare.audit_head WHERE tenant_id = $1 FOR UPDATE`, and when there is no row `INSERT INTO ursitoare.audit_head (tenant_id, seq, hash) VALUES ($1, 0, $2) ON CONFLICT (tenant_id) DO NOTHING` with `GENESIS_HASH` and the select again; `seq = BigInt(row.seq_text) + 1n` (node-pg returns `bigint` as text; the alias must never be `seq` or `at`, because `ORDER BY seq` would then sort the text), `hash = chainHash(row.hash, record)`; `UPDATE ursitoare.audit_head SET seq = $2, hash = $3 WHERE tenant_id = $1`; `INSERT INTO ursitoare.audit_event (tenant_id, seq, at, prev_hash, hash, event_type, actor, target, payload, origin, mk_trace_id, mk_request_id, mk_jti) VALUES ($1, $2, $3::timestamptz, $4, $5, $6, $7::jsonb, $8::jsonb, $9::jsonb, $10, $11, $12, $13)` with `canonicalize` text for the jsonb values (`target` `null` stays SQL NULL) and `at` from `at.toISOString()` of that same Date (never a second `now()` call). Any thrown error goes through `wrapStoreError`. Return `{ seq, hash: hash.toString(\"hex\") }`. Default clock `systemClock` from `src/core`, implementing requirement \"Appending is gapless inside the caller's transaction\""}
